# Knowledge taught to the brain.
#
# Every .json file here is world-shaped — { terms, relations, anchors } — and is
# merged into data/world.json at startup. A file may add terms and may add links
# to terms the world already has; it may not redefine one.
#
# The world under data/ is generic: the ladder every world must have for the
# primitives to bite — thing, place, action, property — the relations, and the
# anchors that name them. It holds no particular thing.
#
# What a particular world contains lives here, one file to a domain: the cities
# and rivers in geography, the sparrows in birds, the hammers in tools. A brain
# built for one purpose takes the packs it needs and leaves the rest, and none
# of them is required — the engine reads the ladder, never a leaf.
